on","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/split(maxSplits:omittingEmptySubsequences:whereSeparator:)":{"title":"split(maxSplits:omittingEmptySubsequences:whereSeparator:)","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/split(maxSplits:omittingEmptySubsequences:whereSeparator:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"split","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxSplits","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"omittingEmptySubsequences","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"whereSeparator","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"ArraySlice","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/split(maxsplits:omittingemptysubsequences:whereseparator:)"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"title":"MaximalCliques","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}]}}}